# Services this fleet runs, one per line; `#` starts a comment.
# Copy it to config/running-products and list the services you want watched.
# Each line has five fields; quote a command that has spaces:
#   <name> <systemd-user-unit> <running-version-command> <wanted-version-command> <auto|manual>
# `bin/jg-running-products.sh check` reports every line and exits 1 when one is behind.
# `refresh` restarts each behind `auto` line with `systemctl --user restart <unit>` and re-reads its version.
# A `manual` line is only reported, and a service no line names is never touched.
# This file starts empty on purpose: naming a service to restart is a decision, never an inference.
